From 7a8bccb5bc4038ea390be2858a478d4ad0a13117 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 00:54:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] capi 1.0.15: a model in one .tar file, and laya_set_codec for
 the weights

All model files are read through laya::model_files. A model path that names a file is mounted
as an uncompressed tar archive in place of the model folder, and a codec set with the new
laya_set_codec decodes the bytes of the weight file while it is read, from a folder or from an
archive. Both are in every build; the API version stays 1 (an eleventh function, nothing
changed in the other ten). tests/capi/test_sources.c and test_sources.py test both.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LAsYHSSgSysMFa8MKPJWgL
